Z||000000||perks88gt||05-18-2001||06:21 PM||||Just bought my third 88 gt with only 32k.  Never seen this on previous two, or the three others in family but there is coolant that is slowly dripping on the passanger side.  Im suspecting that it is the heatercore, but that seems a little pre-mature.  The antifreeze appears to be in good condition, clean and a nice color.  Does anyone have any other ideas?  Is the heater core a hard job?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||05-18-2001||06:37 PM||||Why premature? It's usually caused from inactivity and sedemint in the system.<BR>Not to tough, be done before you know it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||05-18-2001||07:45 PM||||I had to change the heater core on my '86 at about the same mileage.  Fortunately, chaning the heater core on a Fiero is easier than most cars.  Do a search on "heater core".  There should be lots of guidance available.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||05-18-2001||08:22 PM||||Don't be afraid to tackle this one yourself.<BR>ps-your access it from under the frt hood-not under the dash. Takes about half an hour to do the second time, once you have done one before.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||05-18-2001||09:53 PM||||I had this happen in my GT.<BR>The fluid leaked on a friend of mines foot,<BR>he yelled like a girl!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||10
